    <div class="reading-body">
      <p>I am a Computer Science Ph.D. student at Colorado School of Mines in the <strong>MIRROЯLab</strong>, advised by <strong>Dr. Tom Williams</strong>.</p>
      <p>My research centers on <strong>Human-Robot Interaction (HRI)</strong> to design equitable, community-grounded social robotic systems. I study how robots interface with marginalized communities, specifically unhoused populations, and how interactive protocols can respect privacy, preserve human dignity, and avoid paternalistic defaults.</p>
      <p>Prior to Mines, I completed my B.A. in Computer Science at <strong>Colorado College</strong> (GPA 3.92, Steven Janke Award for Outstanding Achievement in CS, Euclid Scholar). My undergraduate research spanned neurosymbolic AI (published at AAAI-25 and PMLR 2025), computational redistricting using MCMC Markov chains, and cultural humanities research for Oxford University Press examining Midwestern Hip Hop subcultures and intersectional feminist frameworks.</p>
